+| 7 | **Agent discovery & routing** — CSTL-native registry, agent cards, zero external deps | ✅ Built and wired live (`src/agent_discovery.rs`, used by every request). **New 2026-09-04**: registration is now dynamic — `Arc<Mutex<AgentRegistry>>` + `purpose=agent_register` wire message (self-signed, upsert by name), verified live; a real LLM agent (`sdk/python/cstl_llm_agent.py`, Ed25519 via `cryptography`) registers and signs its own messages, verified live against the real Rust server (registration, unsigned-rejected, signed-accepted) — actual model-generated content is not verifiable in this sandbox (no `anthropic`/`google-genai` package, no API key here) and is left for the user to confirm on their own machine. **Added 2026-09-05**: `GeminiAgentBrain` (same `generate_relation` interface as `AnthropicAgentBrain`, `--provider anthropic\|gemini\|auto`) — Gemini has a real free tier (key at aistudio.google.com/apikey, no credit card required), unlike the Anthropic API (a Claude Max subscription only covers the chat, not the API), making a real end-to-end LLM-to-server turn reachable by the user at no cost. `google-genai` (the current unified SDK) installs and imports cleanly here; verified live against the real TCP server up to the point blocked by the missing key: `agent_register` succeeds with a real signature, `--provider auto` tries Gemini then falls back to Anthropic, both degrade cleanly (exit code 2, explicit message) since neither `GEMINI_API_KEY` nor `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` exist in this sandbox |
